<section class="page-hero page-hero-simple benefits-hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">FOOD, NOT FADS</span><h1>Good fruit knowledge<br><em>starts with context.</em></h1><p>Fruit can add colour, hydration, fibre and a range of micronutrients to everyday meals. What any fruit contributes depends on the species, serving size, maturity and how it is prepared.</p><a class="button-primary" href="/fruits">Explore fruit profiles <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="simple-hero-side"><span class="big-serif-mark">+F</span><span class="side-rule"></span><p>Variety over<br>miracle claims</p></div></section>
<section class="section-block nutrition-overview"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE BASICS</span><h2>What fruit can contribute</h2><p>These are broad food principles, not nutrient guarantees for every fruit.</p></div></div><div class="nutrition-card-grid"><article class="nutrition-card nutrition-card-berry"><h3>Fibre & texture</h3><p>Whole fruits often contribute dietary fibre, especially when the edible skin and pulp are eaten. Fibre levels differ by fruit and serving; juicing and straining can remove much of the intact structure.</p><a href="/guide/nutrition-without-the-myths">Whole fruit and juice ↗</a></article><article class="nutrition-card nutrition-card-citrus"><h3>Water & freshness</h3><p>Many fruits contain a high proportion of water, which helps explain their refreshing texture. Water content varies, and dried fruit behaves differently from fresh fruit because water has been removed.</p><a href="/storage">Storage and handling ↗</a></article><article class="nutrition-card nutrition-card-leaf"><h3>Vitamins & minerals</h3><p>Different fruits provide different micronutrients. Citrus and many berries are known for vitamin C; orange-fleshed fruit can contribute carotenoids. Exact amounts depend on the specific fruit and portion.</p><a href="/families">Explore by fruit group ↗</a></article><article class="nutrition-card nutrition-card-gold"><h3>Plant pigments</h3><p>Natural pigments can create red, purple, blue, orange and yellow flesh or skin. Pigment chemistry is part of plant biology; colour alone cannot tell you the total nutrient content or a health outcome.</p><a href="/guide/fruit-botany-from-flower-to-fruit">Fruit botany ↗</a></article></div></section>
<section class="nutrition-feature"><div class="nutrition-feature-image"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1490474418585-ba9bad8fd0ea?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1300&q=85" data-wiki-page="Fruit" data-image-fallback="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1619566636858-adf3ef46400b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1300&q=85" alt="A varied bowl of fresh fruit" loading="lazy"></div><div class="nutrition-feature-copy"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">A PRACTICAL RULE</span><h2>Look at the pattern,<br>not a single superfood.</h2><p>A varied diet can include fruits of different colours, textures and forms. Frozen and unsweetened canned fruit can also be useful options; preparation, added sugar, portion and personal tolerance matter.</p><p>Fruit is food, not medicine. This atlas does not promise disease prevention or treatment, and it does not replace tailored advice from a qualified health professional.</p><a href="/guide/nutrition-without-the-myths" class="light-link">Read the full guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="section-block"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">READ A LABEL WITH CARE</span><h2>Why nutrient numbers vary</h2></div></div><div class="plain-two-column"><div><h3>Species and cultivar</h3><p>Two fruits sold under the same common name can differ in sweetness, acidity, edible yield, seeds and nutrient profile. The edible part and preparation method also change what a serving provides.</p></div><div><h3>Maturity and handling</h3><p>Harvest maturity, time in storage, exposure to heat and processing influence taste and some nutrients. Exact values should come from a relevant food-composition database that matches the food and preparation.</p></div></div></section>
